    <system:String x:Key="StrWizardModesBody">Affinity pins a process to selected cores (strict). CPU Sets only prefer selected cores and let Windows schedule more freely (usually friendlier on hybrid CPUs).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="StrWizardModesNote">Hardware monitoring stays OFF and no aggressive optimization is enabled by default. You apply everything explicitly.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="StrWizardStartupTitle">Startup behavior</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="StrWizardNoAdminNote">Administrator rights are optional. The app works without elevation; elevation is only offered where Windows requires it (for example, elevated autostart or protected processes).</system:String>
